## 10.4 Conditional statements and expressions

The conditional statement, call it IF , has the following form in many imperative programming languages:

(10.4) IF : if B then S1 else S2 ,

where B is a boolean expression and S1 and S2 are statements. It is executed as follows: If B is true , execute S1; otherwise execute S2 .

